### Supabase Auth Baseline Checks
### REST Client syntax references: named requests, dotenv vars, prompt vars, request vars.
### Run order: signup -> login -> getUser -> loginWrongPassword

@supabaseUrl = {{$dotenv SUPABASE__URL}}
@supabaseAnonKey = {{$dotenv SUPABASE__PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
@testEmail = test@example.com
@testPassword = Test1234!
@wrongPassword = WrongPass!

### 1) Signup (create user)
# @prompt testEmail Signup email
# @prompt testPassword Signup password
# @name signup
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/signup HTTP/1.1
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 2) Login (password grant)
# @prompt testEmail Login email
# @prompt testPassword Login password
# @name login
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password HTTP/1.1
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 3) Inspect user with access token from login response
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

# @name getUser
GET {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/user HTTP/1.1
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4) Negative test (wrong password)
# @prompt testEmail Negative test email
# @prompt wrongPassword Wrong password value
# @name loginWrongPassword
POST {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password HTTP/1.1
apikey: {{supabaseAnonKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{wrongPassword}}"
}
